1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
I think I have a big deal.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
I think I have a big deal.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Uh...

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Meow.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Hi. There, there.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
All right.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
I'm home.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Welcome back.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Show it to baby. We've got snacks.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
No, thanks. I don't need any...

11
00:02:00,937 --> 00:02:12,237
Chota Baby, what's the matter?

12
00:02:12,577 --> 00:02:15,457
Just trying to think of a good present to make for Dad's Day.

13
00:02:15,877 --> 00:02:16,557
Dad's Day?

14
00:02:18,137 --> 00:02:19,297
A talisman?

15
00:02:19,517 --> 00:02:21,717
It might be a little difficult, but I can do it.

16
00:02:21,937 --> 00:02:23,977
How cool. Allow me to help you out, then.

17
00:02:24,137 --> 00:02:24,757
No, thanks.

18
00:02:26,517 --> 00:02:28,777
This is something I have to do on my own.

19
00:02:28,777 --> 00:02:32,017
Anyway, that's what happened.

20
00:02:32,497 --> 00:02:34,817
Wow, a Father's Day present, huh?

21
00:02:35,237 --> 00:02:36,577
What a thoughtful little guy.

22
00:02:37,337 --> 00:02:40,637
I'm looking forward to seeing what he finally comes up with for me.

23
00:02:41,477 --> 00:02:45,797
Aren't talismans those protective charm-like things I see humans carry around a lot?

24
00:02:46,217 --> 00:02:46,937
You do?

25
00:02:47,637 --> 00:02:49,637
Can you tell if they work or not and to what extent?

26
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:51,457
They don't work at all.

27
00:02:51,917 --> 00:02:54,277
They all go up in flames along with the humans gripping them.

28
00:02:54,497 --> 00:02:56,097
Sounds like a first-hand testimony.

29
00:02:56,097 --> 00:03:01,317
You say that as if all talismans are full of crap, but they actually work quite well with proper magic.

30
00:03:01,937 --> 00:03:02,357
They do?

31
00:03:02,937 --> 00:03:07,377
What I don't get is how a talisman is supposed to show someone you appreciate their yavos.

32
00:03:07,697 --> 00:03:10,257
Okay, I'm confused. Which conversation are you in?

33
00:03:10,517 --> 00:03:13,177
Huh? You know, we're talking about Tits Day.

34
00:03:13,337 --> 00:03:15,837
Uh, seriously? I need to go lie down.

35
00:03:15,837 --> 00:03:32,057
Let me see.

36
00:03:33,317 --> 00:03:34,557
Whoa, that's a lot.

37
00:03:35,037 --> 00:03:36,877
Looks like the official ones are sold out.

38
00:03:37,437 --> 00:03:40,157
The ratings are so low, I can't tell if they're good.

39
00:03:40,157 --> 00:03:46,897
That does it.

40
00:03:49,497 --> 00:03:50,997
Thank you very much.

41
00:03:50,997 --> 00:04:00,657
Okay, first I take a unicorn's horn and wyvern's blood,

42
00:04:00,917 --> 00:04:03,177
ground branches from a tree with a human face,

43
00:04:03,337 --> 00:04:04,897
and one dried blue rose.

44
00:04:05,877 --> 00:04:06,677
That's that.

45
00:04:07,837 --> 00:04:11,437
Now I let everything stew for an hour and wait for the smell to fade.

46
00:04:11,537 --> 00:04:14,017
Then I'll cast the boning spell and it should be complete.

47
00:04:16,417 --> 00:04:18,737
Oh! Shanta Baby, are you okay?

48
00:04:18,737 --> 00:04:20,457
Yeah, I'm fine.

49
00:04:20,657 --> 00:04:22,477
I can help you a tiny bit.

50
00:04:22,797 --> 00:04:23,717
Please don't.

51
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,457
I promise I'm fine.

52
00:04:29,857 --> 00:04:36,197
Okay, try again.

53
00:04:39,017 --> 00:04:45,917
Is everything okay up there?

54
00:04:48,737 --> 00:05:06,797
Nice going, bro.

55
00:05:07,237 --> 00:05:09,477
Man, this new event quest is a beast.

56
00:05:09,997 --> 00:05:11,397
At this rate, I'm gonna get KO'd.

57
00:05:11,817 --> 00:05:12,817
Yeah, you are.

58
00:05:13,137 --> 00:05:14,117
It's not that bad.

59
00:05:14,117 --> 00:05:23,717
Hey, Shanta, what's bugging you?

60
00:05:24,877 --> 00:05:25,177
Hmm?

61
00:05:25,477 --> 00:05:26,477
Um, nothing.

62
00:05:26,757 --> 00:05:28,157
Why do you think I'm bugged?

63
00:05:28,237 --> 00:05:29,357
Just a feeling I get.

64
00:05:32,357 --> 00:05:33,557
To be honest,

65
00:05:33,817 --> 00:05:36,877
I'm trying to make a talisman for a Father's Day present,

66
00:05:37,197 --> 00:05:38,877
but it's not going well.

67
00:05:38,877 --> 00:05:39,757
I see.

68
00:05:40,457 --> 00:05:43,637
I followed the steps written in the grimoire exactly,

69
00:05:43,957 --> 00:05:45,677
so I don't get why it isn't working.

70
00:05:46,277 --> 00:05:48,917
I want to show my Father how good I am at something,

71
00:05:49,157 --> 00:05:50,437
but I keep messing up.

72
00:05:50,757 --> 00:05:53,437
I just need to hurry and become a real-life mage.

73
00:05:55,037 --> 00:05:56,717
Look at it like playing a game.

74
00:05:57,137 --> 00:05:57,757
A game?

75
00:05:58,237 --> 00:06:00,637
When you fight enemies that you know are a higher level,

76
00:06:01,097 --> 00:06:02,977
you don't exactly expect to win, right?

77
00:06:03,537 --> 00:06:05,017
Yeah, that's true.

78
00:06:05,017 --> 00:06:07,677
So, if you really want to defeat them,

79
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:10,797
you should try thinking about the developers' feelings at the time.

80
00:06:11,297 --> 00:06:12,077
The developers?

81
00:06:13,137 --> 00:06:13,577
Yeah.

82
00:06:14,197 --> 00:06:15,557
Games don't just appear out of nowhere.

83
00:06:16,217 --> 00:06:17,377
They're programmed worlds,

84
00:06:17,517 --> 00:06:20,017
and they only operate exactly as the developers intended.

85
00:06:20,877 --> 00:06:23,117
So then, try to imagine what they were feeling

86
00:06:23,117 --> 00:06:24,177
when they designed a level.

87
00:06:24,917 --> 00:06:26,337
What did they want their players to do?

88
00:06:26,757 --> 00:06:28,417
If you can get inside that mindset,

89
00:06:29,197 --> 00:06:30,977
then the instructions on how to clear the game

90
00:06:30,977 --> 00:06:32,357
will become blatantly obvious.

91
00:06:32,357 --> 00:06:35,397
That's the part you always have a problem with, too.

92
00:06:36,337 --> 00:06:38,137
When you're on the developer's side,

93
00:06:38,217 --> 00:06:39,877
you find that it's a huge pen in the A

94
00:06:39,877 --> 00:06:41,937
to figure out ways to mislead your players.

95
00:06:42,757 --> 00:06:44,017
Think like a developer.

96
00:06:44,357 --> 00:06:44,657
Okay.

97
00:06:47,137 --> 00:06:48,357
Thank you so much.

98
00:06:48,557 --> 00:06:50,497
I'll go ahead and give it another try.

99
00:06:50,857 --> 00:06:51,817
Hmm? Hmm.

100
00:06:52,657 --> 00:06:55,297
There has to be some kind of condition required

101
00:06:55,297 --> 00:06:56,977
that's not written in the grimoire.

102
00:06:57,857 --> 00:06:59,417
But what could it be?

103
00:06:59,417 --> 00:06:59,497
Hmm.

104
00:06:59,497 --> 00:06:59,577
Hmm.

105
00:07:02,357 --> 00:07:04,457
All right.

106
00:07:06,597 --> 00:07:07,277
It's done!

107
00:07:08,917 --> 00:07:09,857
Look how I look!

108
00:07:10,117 --> 00:07:11,577
I finished the talisman!

109
00:07:12,217 --> 00:07:12,577
Oh.

110
00:07:13,277 --> 00:07:14,337
Great, Shota Baby.

111
00:07:14,957 --> 00:07:15,917
How'd you do it?

112
00:07:16,177 --> 00:07:18,017
I thought about the person who wrote the grimoire,

113
00:07:18,157 --> 00:07:19,477
and when I looked up where it was written,

114
00:07:19,577 --> 00:07:21,437
I found out it was written in what we call the Dead Sea,

115
00:07:21,537 --> 00:07:22,397
which is below sea level.

116
00:07:22,497 --> 00:07:24,297
So I decided to recreate the very same environment

117
00:07:24,297 --> 00:07:25,637
by increasing the air pressure in my room,

118
00:07:25,757 --> 00:07:27,057
and that's when I discovered the secret.

119
00:07:27,057 --> 00:07:27,577
Hmm.

120
00:07:28,417 --> 00:07:29,557
Never mind, forget it!

121
00:07:29,557 --> 00:07:31,257
Why am I slowly my guns to a demon?

122
00:07:31,257 --> 00:07:31,797
Huh?

123
00:07:31,797 --> 00:07:32,637
Ah!

124
00:07:52,037 --> 00:07:53,437
Did he like the present?

125
00:07:54,677 --> 00:07:56,717
Yeah, sure, but...

126
00:07:58,197 --> 00:08:00,557
he said I need to work harder.

127
00:08:02,717 --> 00:08:05,877
No, Shota, you've worked very hard.

128
00:08:07,277 --> 00:08:09,117
Happy Breast Friends Day!

129
00:08:09,957 --> 00:08:12,517
Hey, you still haven't let me out!

130
00:08:20,517 --> 00:08:22,837
Shoulder massage tickets? What for?

131
00:08:23,197 --> 00:08:24,397
It's a present.

132
00:08:25,037 --> 00:08:27,517
For what? It's not my birthday or anything.

133
00:08:28,237 --> 00:08:29,757
Because it's Father's Day.

134
00:08:29,757 --> 00:08:31,877
Oh, you think I'm a father now?

135
00:08:31,957 --> 00:08:32,837
Mm-hmm.

136
00:08:32,917 --> 00:08:34,157
Like, instead of a mother?

137
00:08:34,237 --> 00:08:34,877
Mm-hmm.

138
00:08:42,877 --> 00:08:44,997
Oh, no, what's the matter, Miss Kobayashi?

139
00:08:45,077 --> 00:08:47,237
Toru, I do believe I've caught a cold.

140
00:08:47,317 --> 00:08:48,277
A cold?

141
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:51,197
I've heard that phrase before, but I still don't understand.

142
00:08:51,277 --> 00:08:52,837
You mean dragons don't catch colds?

143
00:08:53,477 --> 00:08:57,517
There's no way a tiny human virus could survive inside the furnace that is my body.

144
00:08:57,957 --> 00:08:58,877
Must be nice.

145
00:08:59,637 --> 00:09:01,677
Well, time for me to go to work.

146
00:09:02,197 --> 00:09:03,437
Are you well enough to go?

147
00:09:03,437 --> 00:09:04,357
That's cute.

148
00:09:04,437 --> 00:09:07,557
Like, they'd ever let me take off work for something as minor as my...

149
00:09:07,557 --> 00:09:09,837
Whoa.

150
00:09:11,637 --> 00:09:12,757
Miss Kobayashi!

151
00:09:15,077 --> 00:09:15,897
What's that mean?

152
00:09:15,977 --> 00:09:17,957
Should I bang on your chest and blow it in your mouth?

153
00:09:18,197 --> 00:09:19,517
I pray that you won't.

154
00:09:20,357 --> 00:09:23,417
But I won't be able to go into work, so I need to call and let them know.

155
00:09:23,837 --> 00:09:24,997
I'll do it for you!

156
00:09:25,877 --> 00:09:26,597
Oh, no.

157
00:09:26,597 --> 00:09:30,717
Well, let her know I have everything under control, and we hope she feels better.

158
00:09:31,197 --> 00:09:31,597
Okay.

159
00:09:32,157 --> 00:09:33,757
Um, Mr. Takuya?

160
00:09:34,677 --> 00:09:38,917
Miss Kobayashi just took some medicine and already fell asleep, but...

161
00:09:38,917 --> 00:09:40,837
Is there anything else I can do for her?

162
00:09:42,137 --> 00:09:46,497
I'm afraid I don't have much experience with sick humans, so I'm not sure what would help her most.

163
00:09:46,677 --> 00:09:47,037
Hmm.

164
00:09:47,577 --> 00:09:50,437
You could always try to shrink the germs so that they're easier to kill.

165
00:09:50,877 --> 00:09:54,437
I could do that, but I'd likely destroy her body in the process.

166
00:09:55,077 --> 00:09:56,037
Then maybe...

167
00:09:56,037 --> 00:09:58,597
Be her nurse?

168
00:09:58,637 --> 00:09:59,077
That's right.

169
00:09:59,517 --> 00:10:00,197
What's important...

170
00:10:00,197 --> 00:10:01,157
I get it now!

171
00:10:01,397 --> 00:10:04,397
What she needs is a healthy dose of multivitamate power!

172
00:10:05,157 --> 00:10:08,237
Miss Kobayashi needs me, and I will do everything I can to help!

173
00:10:08,477 --> 00:10:11,057
I will protect her body and destroy her viral enemy!

174
00:10:12,097 --> 00:10:13,657
So, um, is that right?

175
00:10:14,017 --> 00:10:15,177
What do nurses do?

176
00:10:15,437 --> 00:10:15,877
Shh!

177
00:10:16,857 --> 00:10:20,057
Why don't you just feed her something that can detoxify her insides?

178
00:10:20,457 --> 00:10:22,177
Like charcoal or some yummy limestone?

179
00:10:22,177 --> 00:10:25,717
Miss Kobayashi isn't a fire dragon, or a brick oven for that matter.

180
00:10:26,037 --> 00:10:30,757
I know plenty of ways to bring about human illness, but I know nothing about curing them.

181
00:10:31,077 --> 00:10:32,757
You should learn to fend them off, too!

182
00:10:33,697 --> 00:10:39,817
All you have to do is feed her something that's easily digested, keep her head cool, and then wipe her sweat when it gets gross.

183
00:10:39,817 --> 00:10:40,317
Ow!

184
00:10:40,317 --> 00:10:41,017
Thank you!

185
00:10:41,017 --> 00:10:45,177
The fact that it takes three attempts to get a reasonable answer says a lot about who my friends are.

186
00:10:45,177 --> 00:10:48,497
I wonder what she means by easily digested.

187
00:10:49,457 --> 00:10:50,217
Let's see.

188
00:10:50,897 --> 00:10:54,417
I can digest just about anything, so it's hard to know it's good.

189
00:10:55,157 --> 00:10:56,037
Rice gruel?

190
00:10:56,357 --> 00:10:58,297
That looks like it's easy to make.

191
00:10:58,597 --> 00:10:59,397
We need yogurt.

192
00:10:59,977 --> 00:11:02,337
I think I saw Kana put some in the fridge.

193
00:11:02,897 --> 00:11:04,957
Udon, gelatin, bananas.

194
00:11:05,837 --> 00:11:06,217
Hmm.

195
00:11:06,217 --> 00:11:07,977
That just leaves something sweet.

196
00:11:08,377 --> 00:11:09,497
Bone apple tea!

197
00:11:09,757 --> 00:11:10,957
Yummy rice gruel!

198
00:11:11,397 --> 00:11:16,377
She went out of her way to make it for me, so I guess it would be rude to say it looks too weird to eat.

199
00:11:17,237 --> 00:11:21,097
Now's probably not the best time to teach her the concept of foods that go well together.

200
00:11:24,217 --> 00:11:25,917
I'm so glad you like it!

201
00:11:27,917 --> 00:11:30,217
Next time, all you have to do is follow the recipe.

202
00:11:30,997 --> 00:11:31,357
Promise?

203
00:11:32,077 --> 00:11:32,477
Okay!

204
00:11:32,477 --> 00:11:39,257
It seems like you're sweating an awful lot.

205
00:11:39,617 --> 00:11:41,217
Would you mind if I wiped it off for you?

206
00:11:41,217 --> 00:11:41,657
Huh?

207
00:11:46,777 --> 00:11:50,617
What is happening?

208
00:11:51,137 --> 00:11:53,077
My heart is racing all of a sudden.

209
00:11:53,077 --> 00:12:02,537
Miss Kobayashi always comes off as such a strong, reliable person.

210
00:12:02,957 --> 00:12:05,497
This is my first time seeing her so vulnerable.

211
00:12:07,577 --> 00:12:09,937
She's gonna be okay, isn't she?

212
00:12:10,597 --> 00:12:13,397
I've known whole villages destroyed by epidemics.

213
00:12:13,817 --> 00:12:16,397
I've seen entire nations wiped out by them, too.

214
00:12:18,537 --> 00:12:19,677
You're gonna get better.

215
00:12:19,677 --> 00:12:21,477
I just wish I knew for sure.

216
00:12:22,297 --> 00:12:24,857
I don't want anything that's precious to me destroyed.

217
00:12:25,457 --> 00:12:27,497
I suppose everything breaks eventually.

218
00:12:28,137 --> 00:12:32,717
That's especially true around me, since I can break just about anything.

219
00:12:35,057 --> 00:12:35,757
All right!

220
00:12:36,377 --> 00:12:37,557
I'm home!

221
00:12:38,357 --> 00:12:39,037
Hello, Kana.

222
00:12:39,237 --> 00:12:39,417
Huh?

223
00:12:39,417 --> 00:12:41,437
Please watch over, Miss Kobayashi.

224
00:12:41,797 --> 00:12:42,337
Mm-hmm.

225
00:12:46,937 --> 00:12:51,877
There are medicines that grant immortality, but I know Miss Kobayashi would never go for those.

226
00:12:52,197 --> 00:12:55,257
I have to at least find something that can cure the illness she has.

227
00:12:55,657 --> 00:12:58,757
That might be harder to find out here, but...

228
00:12:58,757 --> 00:12:59,817
Go do it!

229
00:13:01,017 --> 00:13:02,957
I won't let you down, Miss Kobayashi!

230
00:13:03,437 --> 00:13:04,457
Hang in there!

231
00:13:04,457 --> 00:13:17,817
Oh, man.

232
00:13:18,177 --> 00:13:20,317
I feel so much better after some good rest.

233
00:13:20,857 --> 00:13:21,237
Better?

234
00:13:21,657 --> 00:13:22,577
Are you not well?

235
00:13:22,697 --> 00:13:25,957
I'll be okay after I get some medicine and some sleep for a few days.

236
00:13:26,217 --> 00:13:27,097
That's amazing!

237
00:13:27,657 --> 00:13:27,897
Hmm?

238
00:13:28,217 --> 00:13:28,937
Where's Toru?

239
00:13:30,937 --> 00:13:31,597
There you are.

240
00:13:31,597 --> 00:13:34,777
What's the matter?

241
00:13:35,217 --> 00:13:36,137
You look exhausted.

242
00:13:37,237 --> 00:13:38,077
Here you go.

243
00:13:38,937 --> 00:13:40,337
I searched everywhere.

244
00:13:41,717 --> 00:13:43,117
Um, what is that?

245
00:13:43,857 --> 00:13:46,977
It's medicine that's supposed to be very effective for cults.

246
00:13:47,357 --> 00:13:48,597
Okay, but is it safe?

247
00:13:48,897 --> 00:13:50,597
There's nothing weird like chicken breath is...

248
00:13:52,977 --> 00:13:55,417
Hmm.

249
00:13:58,057 --> 00:13:58,537
Thanks.

250
00:13:58,677 --> 00:13:59,237
I'll try them.

251
00:13:59,237 --> 00:13:59,357
Hmm.

252
00:14:01,597 --> 00:14:08,077
They work.

253
00:14:09,137 --> 00:14:10,077
You mean that?

254
00:14:10,757 --> 00:14:11,237
Really?

255
00:14:12,077 --> 00:14:12,657
Mm-hmm.

256
00:14:12,817 --> 00:14:13,677
This is incredible.

257
00:14:14,837 --> 00:14:16,237
Oh, thank goodness!

258
00:14:16,457 --> 00:14:16,877
Honestly?

259
00:14:17,157 --> 00:14:17,897
I'm worried about you.

260
00:14:18,017 --> 00:14:19,577
I don't know if it's working or not.

261
00:14:19,737 --> 00:14:20,497
That would work.

262
00:14:21,357 --> 00:14:24,937
But that look on her face has to be some of the best medicine in the world.

263
00:14:27,177 --> 00:14:28,057
Hey, Toru?

264
00:14:28,257 --> 00:14:28,797
Thank you.

265
00:14:28,797 --> 00:14:28,857
Thank you.

266
00:14:28,857 --> 00:14:38,217
What the heck is out of my head and growing out of my face?

267
00:14:38,397 --> 00:14:39,017
Uh-oh.

268
00:14:39,457 --> 00:14:40,837
Maybe it's a side effect?

269
00:14:41,197 --> 00:14:43,317
The medicine was for beast bulk.

270
00:14:43,917 --> 00:14:45,337
